Model weights

Telmo's code and packages contain no model weights. The `telmo` command downloads them when
asked, under their own licences. The speech models come from Hugging Face, and the disfluency
tagger comes from this repository's releases.

- Granite Speech 5.0 470M TurboCTC by IBM,
  https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-speech-5.0-470m-turboctc,
  Apache License, Version 2.0.
- Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 by NVIDIA, https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3,
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  Packs converted from it are adaptations of NVIDIA's work under the same licence.
- The disfluency tagger, disfluency-tagger-1-q8_0.pack, under the MIT License or the Apache
  License, Version 2.0, at your option. It is fine-tuned from Ettin encoder 68M by Johns Hopkins
  University's Center for Language and Speech Processing,
  https://huggingface.co/jhu-clsp/ettin-encoder-68m, MIT License, whose notice follows. It was
  trained on the disfluency annotations of the AMI Meeting Corpus (Carletta et al., 2005),
  https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/corpus/, Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Ettin encoder 68M's licence, from https://github.com/jhu-clsp/ettin-encoder-vs-decoder

