Test data in the repository

The repository's tests/goldens directory (left out of the published package) holds audio and
model outputs used to check Telmo against the reference implementations.

- Audio from the LibriSpeech ASR corpus, (c) 2014 Vassil Panayotov, https://www.openslr.org/12,
  CC BY 4.0.
- Audio from FLEURS by Google, https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/fleurs, CC BY 4.0.
- Tensors that Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 computed on those clips, CC BY 4.0, and tensors that
  Granite Speech 5.0 470M TurboCTC computed on them, under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
- Token ids that Ettin encoder 68M's tokenizer gives made-up strings, MIT License, whose notice
  is above.

The README in each directory under tests/goldens gives the details.

Text normalization

examples/wer ports the English and multilingual text normalizers of OpenAI's Whisper
(https://github.com/openai/whisper, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI) and the Open ASR
Leaderboard's changes to them (https://github.com/huggingface/open_asr_leaderboard, Apache
License, Version 2.0), with tables generated from them.
